# KubeVerse desktop shell - environment configuration template.
# Copy the variable(s) you need into your real shell/CI environment before
# launching KubeVerse. This file is never read automatically - it exists
# only as safe, credential-free documentation of what can be configured.
# Never commit a real value here.

# Required for "Continue with Google" to be available at all. Without it,
# the sign-in button is simply not offered - KubeVerse still launches and
# works fully without it (Google identity is optional; see
# KUBEVERSE_MASTER_SPEC.md §7).
#
# How to get a real value:
#   1. Create (or reuse) a project in https://console.cloud.google.com/
#   2. Configure the OAuth consent screen (External or Internal, as fits
#      your use case).
#   3. Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID with application type "Desktop app".
#   4. Copy the Client ID (NOT the client secret - KubeVerse never uses one,
#      by design; see googleAuth.js's own comments for why a Desktop app
#      OAuth client doesn't need it here).
#
# This value is not a secret - it identifies your OAuth client, not a
# credential that grants access on its own - but it is still specific to
# your own Google Cloud project, so no real value is provided here.
KUBEVERSE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
